# `str` is a BUILTIN FUNCTION name, never reserved (appendix-b-keywords.md:38);
# the string type is spelled `string` (03-types.md:81, appendix-b-keywords.md:18-20).
# `str` is ALSO tychoc0's internal spelling of the string type, so tychoc0 used to
# hand a written `str` annotation straight back as the real type and ACCEPT this
# program while tychoc rejected it -- a fail-open accept/reject divergence on the
# one property the spec makes normative (00-conventions.md §1.3,
# appendix-f-impl-defined.md:63-64). Both compilers must reject.
# Same root cause / same check as reject/void_as_type.ty and reject/char_as_type.ty
# (the internal-spelling guard in parse_type_d); one file per name because the
# compiler stops at the first error.
fn main():
    x: str = "h"
    println(x)
